# super-fr is a Skill: it is cloned onto every consumer's machine by the
# marketplace rsync, so a committed binary inflates every install forever and
# needs a history rewrite to remove. Presentation media lives OUTSIDE the repo
# and is resolved through an asset manifest; this file is only the backstop for
# when that discipline slips.
#
# Note: version-1/diagrams/ already holds 17 tracked PNGs that predate this
# rule. Ignoring a pattern does not untrack what is already tracked — these
# lines stop NEW additions; excising the existing ones is a separate decision,
# since reclaiming the bytes needs a history rewrite.

# terminal recordings
*.cast

# video
*.mp4
*.webm
*.mov

# raster stills
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.webp

# exported decks
*.pptx
*.pdf
